     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     Use this option to add a drive through software after you install 
     a drive or rank of drives in the array subsystem (or integrated 
     array).  
 
     NOTE:  A procedure for adding a drive is included in the help 
            screens following the explanation of option.
 
 
     WHAT "ADD" MEANS:  Adding a drive through software causes the 
     array controller to change the drive status from "Non-existent" 
     (1) to "Spare" (2), thus making the drive available for you to 
     create a logical unit.  
 
     WHEN TO ADD A DRIVE:  You do NOT need to use this option (unless you 
     mistakenly delete a drive).  It is a feature for non-NCR array 
     subsystems.
 
 
 
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     PROCEDURE -- ADDING A DRIVE
 
     NOTE:  To add a drive, you must first install a drive or 
            rank of drives in the array subsystem (or integrated
            array).
 
     1.   Select the drive you want to add by pressing the arrow keys.
 
     2.   Press "a" to add the drive.
 
     3.   Repeat steps 1 - 2 until you have added all the drives
          you want.
